1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:02,740
Utah, Mudron,

2
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:16,660
Mudron!

3
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:23,090
Ohhhhhhhh!!!

4
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,257
It seems I was right
about the world's speed

5
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,497
and power exceeding that of Star Platinum,

6
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,540
So,

7
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,640
there's nothing left to do
but bring this game to an end.

8
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,477
It should have been done ages ago,

9
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,913
but I'll finally be rid of
you Joestars once and for all.

10
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:44,640
Using the power of my stand, I
will send you all into oblivion!

11
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,380
Now the world will stop time itself!

12
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:09,877
At the end of the day, they'll be gone.

13
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,617
I ruined my life.

14
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,040
And I brought you to it.

15
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:19,280
But I don't know what a must.

16
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:24,760
I'm still seeing the fate.

17
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,560
The fate of a mountain.

18
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,460
End of the day.

19
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:40,400
Jotaro, your exasperating family line is
just moments away from being eradicated.

20
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,460
My hundred year struggle with
the Josars ends with you.

21
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:45,870
Begone!

22
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,160
He moved his finger, but how?

23
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,520
What's going on?

24
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,586
He shouldn't be able to
think, let alone move.

25
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,177
Wait, there's no way.

26
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:11,420
Is his power

27
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:16,660
the same as the world's?

28
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,620
Your stand has a lot in
common with my Star Platinum.

29
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,280
Did he mean the world and Star
Platinum are the same type of stand?

30
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,430
Damn it.

31
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:36,140
Can you see me right now?

32
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,911
Are you consciously moving, or
is it an involuntary twitch?

33
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,200
Okay, time's up.

34
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,400
Jotaro, could you see me?

35
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,820
Must I repeat?

36
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,412
I asked if you could follow my movements!

37
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,580
See what?

38
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,212
You're not making sense.

39
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,516
Need to have your eyes checked, D .O.

40
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,020
Just you wait!

41
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,514
You can't run forever!

42
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:20,799
Seeing me isn't going to do you any
good when time is standing still!

43
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:25,096
If your Stone does bear
similarities to mine, prove it!

44
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,400
I want to see just how
much we have in common!

45
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,510
Yes.

46
00:04:30,593 --> 00:04:34,279
It's been six months since I began
to grasp the art of stopping time.

47
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:41,160
To test the world's speed and power,

48
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:45,917
I commanded my servant to take
aim point-blank, right at my back.

49
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,800
And for a moment, it looked as
though time itself had stood still.

50
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,780
I thought for sure I was hallucinating.

51
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:58,997
It seemed like the vision a boxer has when
his opponent's punches linger in mid-air.

52
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,400
That second felt like an eternity.

53
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,580
But I wasn't simply imagining things.

54
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:07,577
My stand was actually
able to move between the

55
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,307
hovering bullets that
were suspended in time.

56
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,620
And it could grasp them.

57
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,000
Yes, Lord D .O.

58
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:23,017
You are well on your way to
being the master of time.

59
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:27,397
The next step is willing yourself to
move through the realm of frozen time.

60
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,892
It must happen as naturally as breathing,

61
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:34,160
or as nonchalantly as snapping a
pencil betwixt your mighty fingers.

62
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:37,008
You must think of it
as completely ordinary.

63
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:40,217
The most important thing is
having faith in yourself.

64
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:44,418
It's imperative that you find the
mental fortitude to steal your mind.

65
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,440
You are the one true ruler of this world!

66
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:51,644
Controlling time should
be second nature to you!

67
00:05:54,480 --> 00:06:00,120
Then one day, I sensed the wheels of time
and the world interlock at long last.

68
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:05,800
Like a ray of clarity dispersing the
shadows in my mind, a revelation befell me.

69
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:12,080
I was Dio, and my destiny was to surpass
all living things, including stand-users!

70
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:17,597
I can stop time for five seconds, And the
time limit keeps extending by the day now!

71
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:21,057
Jotaro, you're about to
experience just how weak you are.

72
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:23,420
Time to make good on my promise!

73
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,780
The world grinds to a halt.

74
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,000
I see you planted a magnet.

75
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:03,717
Must have been when we
were exchanging glows.

76
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,682
It looks like a wallet magnet or
one picked from a pocket planner.

77
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,680
I have to admit, you had me fooled.

78
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,568
You're a clever boy indeed.

79
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,700
But, if you have to resort
to inane tricks like that?

80
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:20,297
It only proves that you can't move.

81
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:22,086
while time is standing still.

82
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,457
You've only postponed the
inevitable by a few seconds.

83
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:26,540
This is the end!

84
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,120
Die, Jotaro!

85
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,390
What?

86
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,510
What?

87
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:46,000
Oh, no, he's moving.

88
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:49,780
What nerve, although he
can only do it briefly.

89
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,317
The magnet wasn't meant to
make me think he could move.

90
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,517
It was made to make me think he couldn't.

91
00:07:55,600 --> 00:08:00,137
Damn it, it was a trap designed
to lure me in, and I fell for it.

92
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:03,749
The key is believing that your
power is completely ordinary.

93
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,557
Disgusting, to think that
my domain could be invaded,

94
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:10,140
And by one of the Joestars, no less!

95
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,020
It's infuriating!

96
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,375
I was able to move for a second there.

97
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,638
That's a good sign.

98
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,900
Even so, that's not much.

99
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:34,298
It would only give me enough
time for a single punch.

100
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,197
You there woman?

101
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:50,000
How about you make yourself
useful and fetch me my leg!

102
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,197
Bring it here this instant!

103
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:57,157
Imagine you're a flight attendant bringing
caviar to a passenger in first class!

104
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,828
If it gets you here faster!

105
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,737
Well that's good to know!

106
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:11,761
Seems I'll have to blow your head
off to do any significant damage!

107
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,090
Bastard!

108
00:09:14,173 --> 00:09:17,191
You've already siphoned off
enough energy to heal yourself!

109
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:22,479
It's like that gaping hole I opened
in your gut was never even there!

110
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:29,317
Your eyes followed me even
while time was frozen!

111
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,317
Which confirms that you
can see my movements?

112
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:33,871
Isn't that right, Jotaro?

113
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,957
Nervous yet, sweetheart? Not at all.

114
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:41,037
Kakyoin, did you quite the favor?

115
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,017
Because of his brilliant mind.

116
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,497
He was able to correctly
deduce the world's secret.

117
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,817
And because he passed
that knowledge along,

118
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:50,057
You figured out that I
could stop time at will?

119
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:53,140
and worked until you learned
how to do it yourself.

120
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,810
Then again,

121
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:57,177
you haven't had as much
training as I have,

122
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:01,597
so I'm curious to know exactly how
long you can move while time is frozen.

123
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,740
Two seconds? Or maybe three?

124
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,717
Or perhaps you can move
five seconds like me,

125
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:10,177
but you're pretending you can't
to gain some kind of an advantage.

126
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:11,090
Clever.

127
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:14,880
Which is it?

128
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:16,800
This isn't good.

129
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:21,217
I could probably move longer if I
was able to get some practice in.

130
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:24,580
But as it stands, the
best I can do is a second.

131
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:30,420
If I was forced to make a guess, I'd
say you could only move for a second.

132
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:35,100
Be that as it may, you've still
managed to infiltrate my world.

133
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:39,337
Only a fool would risk approaching
you now, and though I'm many things,

134
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:41,597
a fool wouldn't be considered one of them.

135
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:45,856
While it's achingly clear that my
advantage over you is overwhelming...

136
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,900
I've still devised a way to execute you!

137
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:54,041
So regardless of how long you can move in
my world, you'll never escape your demise!

138
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,012
You're white as a sheet.

139
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,886
Do these bring back memories?

140
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,877
Do they remind you that
you're going to die a death

141
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,901
even more horrific than
your pathetic grandfather?

142
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,500
Screw this bastard.

143
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,957
How the hell does he come
up with this kind of shit?

144
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,275
I need to be careful.

145
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:13,040
There is no escape!

146
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,020
The world!

147
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:23,820
Five seconds left.

148
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:33,320
Do you think your star platinum can deflect
all of the knives once time resumes?

149
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:38,405
If I were a betting man, I'd give that
plan a one in a million chance of working.

150
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:39,680
Four seconds!

151
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:47,011
It must be terrifying to stare Death
in the face and be helpless to stop it!

152
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:48,909
Only three seconds remain!

153
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,860
You're down to two seconds?

154
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,966
Are you telling me that's
the best you've got?

155
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:07,682
That's just more evidence of your ineptitude
in the presence of one such as myself.

156
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,000
One second left to go.

157
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:13,090
Zero.

158
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,920
It's over.

159
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,340
But one can never be too careful.

160
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,040
Now, to be perfectly honest,

161
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:42,145
I'm relieved I was able to do
away with you so quickly, Chotaro.

162
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:44,720
I have to say,

163
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:49,901
I never would have thought that you'd have
the power to infiltrate my perfect world.

164
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,180
Now, let's see.

165
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:54,051
A fitting analogy would be the automobile.

166
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:58,048
Useful machines until the roads
become clogged with them all.

167
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:04,900
Sorry, but the Mantle of Master
of Time is reserved for me alone.

168
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,740
Good grief.

169
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,821
He'd throw enough knives or what?

170
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:27,215
I mean he'd turn my favorite
uniform into Swiss cheese.

171
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:34,337
Well I'm glad I decided to stuff my
clothes with magazines I figured it was

172
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:38,597
only a matter of time before he tried
throwing weapons but I didn't expect

173
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:44,557
that many my best bet right now is to
play possum and wait for a chance to

174
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:50,177
take dio by surprise since he can
regenerate I've got to Bash his brains in,

175
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,672
or else he'll never die.

176
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:02,221
I believe I'll do one more
check for good measure.

177
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:05,397
The Joestars have a way of
coming back from the dead.

178
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,833
And there's a chance Jotaro
is putting on this death act.

179
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,460
I need to make sure he's gone.

180
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,720
For good.

181
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:17,800
I'll use this.

182
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,740
To sever that troublesome head of his!

183
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,500
It's time for you to die!

184
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:32,990
Shotaro!

185
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:47,320
The only one dying here is you!

186
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:57,360
You're the one who's gonna die! Polnareff!

187
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,000
Time has stopped.

188
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,399
Let's get a good look at your face.

189
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,680
I see.

190
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,180
It's Polnareff.

191
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:18,020
And now time will resume.

192
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:19,990
No!

193
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:24,460
What a shame, Polnareff.

194
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,933
You were so close, but dropped the ball.

195
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:30,017
If you'd lunged with more
force behind your attack,

196
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,917
you could have eviscerated my brain?

197
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,941
beyond the point of regeneration.

198
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,520
You bastard.

199
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,660
It's not over yet.

200
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:42,760
When will you all accept
that you cannot kill me?

201
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:46,357
You are nothing more than pawns
destined to be put in check.

202
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:51,360
Your death brings about the end of
the Joestar's tragic Egyptian journey.

203
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:52,710
Damn it.

204
00:15:52,793 --> 00:15:55,898
If I don't do something,
Polnareff's as good as dead.

205
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,477
I was gonna keep up this act until I had a

206
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:02,501
chance to catch him off
guard and crush his skull.

207
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:06,975
But saving Polnareff from this United
freak is more important right now.

208
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:08,984
It's not gonna be easy, though.

209
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:12,157
He won't make the mistake of
crossing into Star Platinum's range,

210
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:15,416
so it'll just end up like
the last time he trapped me.

211
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,546
Whatever I do, I can't
let him know I'm alive.

212
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,477
As long as he thinks I'm dead,

213
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:24,795
I have the element of surprise, which
gives me a chance to get in close.

214
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:27,807
Strange how things end
up coming full circle.

215
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:31,617
One minute I'm trying to will myself
to move through a world of frozen time,

216
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:35,524
and the next I'm doing everything
I can to stay completely still.

217
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:38,260
Enjoy your journey to the afterlife!

218
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,040
Damn you, Jotaro!

219
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:50,520
Was he alive all along?

220
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,506
At the very least, he
seems to be coming, too.

221
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:56,710
Hold it!

222
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,500
This is the police!

223
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,057
You try anything funny and we will shoot!

224
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:03,081
Slowly put your hands in the air!

225
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,400
Ah, what impeccable timing.

226
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:14,257
If you wouldn't mind, there's
somebody I'd like for you to shoot.

227
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:19,000
Do you see that man lying on the
ground shoot his leg or torso?

228
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:22,450
That's right.

229
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:24,793
Line up the shot and let the bullet fly.

230
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:35,760
I thought I heard Jotaro
make a sound a moment ago,

231
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:38,507
but I guess my mind was
playing tricks on me.

232
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:45,937
Could he be any more demented?

233
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,917
He's at least lost interest in Polnareff,

234
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,897
but now that his attention's back
on me, he's even more suspicious.

235
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,940
He's not gonna rest
until he's sure I'm dead.

236
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:57,937
Things just got a lot harder.

237
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,697
I know why.

238
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,486
Don't we check his breathing?

239
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:05,997
No luck.

240
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:11,360
He's not breathing, but there's
no way to hide his heartbeat.

241
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,020
Shit, this hurts.

242
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:32,457
If I black out, everything we've been
through will have been for nothing.

243
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:35,540
Dying because I used my
own stand to stop my heart.

244
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:37,000
It'd be ironic.

245
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,940
In a morbid kind of way.

246
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:47,777
And sure enough there's no
heartbeat what do you know i

247
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:50,537
suppose the thought of him being
alive was just a figment of my

248
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:55,617
imagination though stranger things
have happened so i should still

249
00:18:55,700 --> 00:19:00,440
probably lop off his head to be
sure that's not a problem is it

250
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,030
What?

251
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,120
I have to stop time again!

252
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,600
The world!

253
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,080
I gotta hand it to you.

254
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,317
You really put me through hell back there.

255
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:32,417
You're not stopping time or
leaving with your skull intact.

256
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,330
Got it?

257
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,630
No!

258
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,860
This can't be happening to me!

259
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:45,720
It took long enough.

260
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:49,904
I finally got to run my fist
straight through his demented skull.

261
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:55,381
But that walking cesspool of evil lived at
the bottom of the sea for over a century.

262
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,757
I can't be sure that attack killed him.

263
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:00,820
It's a bit too early
to take a victory lap.

264
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,820
I will annihilate you!

265
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,320
What the hell?

266
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:14,160
I can't move!

267
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,800
Jotaro, what did you do to me?

268
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:19,300
I don't have control over my legs!

269
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:20,880
I can't even stand!

270
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,480
My head!

271
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,133
The pain is unbearable!

272
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:27,530
Unbearable.

273
00:20:27,613 --> 00:20:28,860
I think I'm going to vomit.

274
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,865
This can't be happening to me.

275
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,920
I'm the pinnacle of perfection.

276
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:38,197
He actually damaged my
brain and paralyzed my legs.

277
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,640
Shit, shit, shit.

278
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,919
I've got to find a way out of here.

279
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:49,157
I've doused you with
gasoline so you can't hide.

280
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:52,317
Normally I would hate to kick a
guy when he's down on his luck.

281
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,920
But, with you, I don't give a damn.

282
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:58,497
You killed my friends and
countless innocent bystanders.

283
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:00,300
So don't expect any mercy.

284
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:14,160
Come forth, the world!

285
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:24,520
If I can just make it a little farther

286
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:32,560
And now time will flow as usual

287
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:41,737
While he had his ear to the ground he
was also listening for any nearby cars?

288
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,217
Clever, but...

289
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:45,594
Bastard's not getting away that easily!

290
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:57,490
Almost...

291
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,860
Keep going!

292
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:01,680
That's it!

293
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:03,740
I'm almost there!

294
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:07,620
And where do you think you're going?

295
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:09,625
We've got unfinished business.

296
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:14,040
It's over, Dio.

297
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,460
Time to accept it.

298
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,480
The world! Free!

299
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,980
You fell for it, Jotaro!

300
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:48,700
Now my victory is all but assured!

301
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:52,340
Once again, my genius
has triumphed over you!

302
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:54,680
Doesn't this street look familiar?

303
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:02,240
This street...

304
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:04,400
What have I done?

305
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,117
You failed.

306
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:13,260
This was my escape route
to your grandfather.

307
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:15,400
And now his blood is mine!

308
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:21,240
T .O.

309
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:23,120
You're dead!

310
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,030
Jotaro.

311
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:30,980
It's been quite the journey, eh, my boy?

312
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:34,097
The blood of the Joestars
courses through my veins!

313
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:37,057
The blood of the Joestars
courses through my veins!

314
00:23:37,140 --> 00:23:41,611
This whole thing might have ended
differently, but you wouldn't piss me off.
